---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "../styles/global.css";
import { readFileSync } from "node:fs";
import { resolve } from "node:path";

// Build-time data files resolve from the project root (process.cwd() is the website/ dir).
const serverJson = JSON.parse(readFileSync(resolve(process.cwd(), "../server.json"), "utf-8"));
const version = serverJson.version;

const runnerCargoCmd = "cargo install mirroir-run";
const runnerBrewCmd = "brew install jfarcand/tap/mirroir-run";
const maestroCmd = "mirroir-run import maestro flows/*.yaml -o .mirroir/apps/shop/scenarios --app com.example.shop=Shop";
const actionSnippet = `- uses: jfarcand/mirroir-mcp/actions/setup-mirroir-run@main
  with:
    version: latest
- run: mirroir-run`;
---

<Layout
  title="mirroir-mcp reference: MCP tools and mirroir-run commands"
  description="Every mirroir-mcp MCP tool for driving a real iPhone, and the mirroir-run commands that replay scenarios on web, iOS and CI."
  softwareVersion={version}
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <h1>Reference</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">The MCP tools your agent gets, and the <code>mirroir-run</code> commands that replay scenarios.</p>
    <ul class="page-toc">
      <li><a href="#tools">Tools</a></li>
      <li><a href="#mirroir-run">mirroir-run</a></li>
      <li><a href="#more">More docs</a></li>
    </ul>
  </header>

  <main>
  <!-- What it does -->
  <section id="tools">
    <h2>What mirroir-mcp can do</h2>
    <p>39 tools exposed as an MCP server.</p>

    <div class="tool-grid">
      <div class="tool-category cat-touch">
        <h3>Touch</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><code>tap</code> <span>Tap visible text, or a point from describe_screen</span></li>
          <li><code>double_tap</code> <span>Double-tap for zoom or text selection</span></li>
          <li><code>long_press</code> <span>Hold for context menus</span></li>
          <li><code>swipe</code> <span>Quick flick between two points</span></li>
          <li><code>drag</code> <span>Slow drag for sliders and icons</span></li>
          <li><code>touch</code> <span>Hold a finger across calls for joysticks and press-and-hold</span></li>
          <li><code>pinch</code> <span>Two-finger pinch to zoom</span></li>
          <li><code>rotate</code> <span>Two-finger rotation</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="tool-category cat-input">
        <h3>Input</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><code>type_text</code> <span>Type text via virtual keyboard</span></li>
          <li><code>press_key</code> <span>Send special keys with modifiers</span></li>
          <li><code>shake</code> <span>Shake gesture for undo or dev menus</span></li>
          <li><code>hold_keys</code> <span>Hold keys during a mouse drag for keyboard-and-mouse games</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="tool-category cat-observe">
        <h3>Observe</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><code>screenshot</code> <span>Capture screen as PNG</span></li>
          <li><code>describe_screen</code> <span>OCR or LLM vision with tap coordinates</span></li>
          <li><code>classify_screen</code> <span>Group screen elements into UI components with an AI model</span></li>
          <li><code>start_recording</code> <span>Begin video recording</span></li>
          <li><code>stop_recording</code> <span>End recording, get file path</span></li>
          <li><code>get_orientation</code> <span>Portrait or landscape</span></li>
          <li><code>status</code> <span>Connection and device readiness</span></li>
          <li><code>check_health</code> <span>Full setup diagnostic</span></li>
          <li><code>calibrate_component</code> <span>Test UI component definitions against live screen</span></li>
          <li><code>list_targets</code> <span>List configured automation targets</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="tool-category cat-navigate">
        <h3>Navigate</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><code>launch_app</code> <span>Open app by name via Spotlight</span></li>
          <li><code>open_url</code> <span>Open URL in Safari</span></li>
          <li><code>press_home</code> <span>Return to home screen</span></li>
          <li><code>press_app_switcher</code> <span>Show recent apps</span></li>
          <li><code>press_back</code> <span>Go back via the OCR-detected back chevron</span></li>
          <li><code>spotlight</code> <span>Open Spotlight search</span></li>
          <li><code>scroll_to</code> <span>Scroll until element visible via OCR</span></li>
          <li><code>reset_app</code> <span>Force-quit app via App Switcher</span></li>
          <li><code>set_network</code> <span>Toggle airplane, Wi-Fi, cellular</span></li>
          <li><code>measure</code> <span>Time screen transitions</span></li>
          <li><code>run_steps</code> <span>Run several steps in one call, stopping at the first failure</span></li>
          <li><code>generate_skill</code> <span>Autonomous BFS exploration &rarr; navigation graph &rarr; SKILL.md bundle</span></li>
          <li><code>list_skills</code> <span>List available skills</span></li>
          <li><code>get_skill</code> <span>Read skill with env substitution + compilation status</span></li>
          <li><code>record_step</code> <span>Record a compiled step during execution</span></li>
          <li><code>save_compiled</code> <span>Save compiled .json for zero-OCR replay</span></li>
          <li><code>switch_target</code> <span>Switch active automation target</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- mirroir-run: cross-platform replay -->
  <section id="mirroir-run">
    <h2>Replay anywhere with <code>mirroir-run</code></h2>
    <p>
      <strong>mirroir-run</strong> replays the same scenarios beyond the iPhone: web pages through Playwright (Chromium, Firefox, WebKit), processes and HTTP natively, and iOS blocks through <code>mirroir-mcp</code>. One YAML file can drive a browser and a phone and check that they show the same thing &mdash; and its web, process, and HTTP steps run on Linux CI.
    </p>

    <div class="pipeline-grid">
      <div class="pipeline-step">
        <div class="pipeline-icon">1</div>
        <h3>Validate</h3>
        <p>Check a scenario against the grammar before anything runs.</p>
        <div class="pipeline-cmd">
          <code>mirroir-run --validate scenario.yaml</code>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="pipeline-step">
        <div class="pipeline-icon">2</div>
        <h3>Compile</h3>
        <p>Write the Playwright spec without running it, for review.</p>
        <div class="pipeline-cmd">
          <code>mirroir-run --emit playwright scenario.yaml</code>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="pipeline-step">
        <div class="pipeline-icon">3</div>
        <h3>Run</h3>
        <p>Run one scenario: web in Playwright, iOS through <code>mirroir-mcp</code>.</p>
        <div class="pipeline-cmd">
          <code>mirroir-run --run-scenario scenario.yaml</code>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="pipeline-step">
        <div class="pipeline-icon">4</div>
        <h3>Sample</h3>
        <p>Boot once, run several scenarios, aggregate the verdicts.</p>
        <div class="pipeline-cmd">
          <code>mirroir-run --sample samples/foo</code>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="pipeline-step">
        <div class="pipeline-icon">5</div>
        <h3>Diff</h3>
        <p>Compare two text outputs for drift, exit-coded for CI.</p>
        <div class="pipeline-cmd">
          <code>mirroir-run --diff-text a.txt b.txt</code>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p>
      Every primitive in one run: <a href="https://github.com/jfarcand/mirroir-mcp/tree/main/runner/samples/mega-sample" rel="noopener noreferrer"><code>runner/samples/mega-sample/</code></a>. Scenario grammar, judge profiles, and CI setup: <a href="https://github.com/jfarcand/mirroir-mcp/tree/main/runner/docs" rel="noopener noreferrer"><code>runner/docs/</code></a> and <a href="https://github.com/jfarcand/mirroir-mcp/blob/main/docs/web-and-ios.md" rel="noopener noreferrer">Web and iOS in one scenario</a>.
    </p>

    <p class="install-hint">Install the runner:</p>
    <div class="install-block">
      <code><span class="prompt">$</span> {runnerCargoCmd}</code>
      <button class="copy-btn" data-copy={runnerCargoCmd}>Copy</button>
    </div>
    <p class="alt-install">or via Homebrew:</p>
    <div class="install-block install-block-alt">
      <code><span class="prompt">$</span> {runnerBrewCmd}</code>
      <button class="copy-btn" data-copy={runnerBrewCmd}>Copy</button>
    </div>
    <p class="alt-install">
      or grab a prebuilt binary for macOS / Linux / Windows from the <a href="https://github.com/jfarcand/mirroir-mcp/releases" rel="noopener noreferrer"><code>runner-v*</code> releases</a>.
    </p>

    <h3 class="compare-title">In GitHub Actions</h3>
    <p>
      <a href="https://github.com/jfarcand/mirroir-mcp/tree/main/actions/setup-mirroir-run" rel="noopener noreferrer"><code>setup-mirroir-run</code></a> installs the released binary on Linux, macOS or Windows, verifies its SHA-256 and adds it to <code>PATH</code>.
    </p>
    <pre class="snippet"><code>{actionSnippet}</code></pre>

    <h3 class="compare-title">Bring your Maestro flows</h3>
    <p>
      Maestro flows run on a real, stock iPhone. Each flow becomes an <code>.ios.yaml</code> scenario; commands mirroir cannot run faithfully fail the import with their file and line. Full mapping: <a href="https://github.com/jfarcand/mirroir-mcp/blob/main/runner/docs/maestro-import.md" rel="noopener noreferrer"><code>maestro-import.md</code></a>.
    </p>
    <div class="install-block">
      <code><span class="prompt">$</span> {maestroCmd}</code>
      <button class="copy-btn" data-copy={maestroCmd}>Copy</button>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- More docs -->
  <section id="more">
    <h2>More documentation</h2>
    <p>
      Setup, permissions, targets and troubleshooting are in the <a href="https://github.com/jfarcand/mirroir-mcp#readme" rel="noopener noreferrer">README</a>; guides are in <a href="https://github.com/jfarcand/mirroir-mcp/tree/main/docs" rel="noopener noreferrer"><code>docs/</code></a>.
    </p>
  </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
